{"question_id": "q01", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "A coding harness fixes repository bugs by wrapping a language model with three core tools\u2014a file editor, a shell, and a test runner\u2014so the model can edit code, run commands, and verify fixes automatically; the harness then scores the resulting patches [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-13", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "nm-01", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4760, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q02", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "ToolBench measures **argument correctness and call order** when a model calls a function [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus"], "tokens": 2834, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q03", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a peer-reviewed paper on multi-agent coordination, a **dispatcher** component prevents duplication by assigning each subtask to a distinct worker while a planner broadcasts a shared plan to all agents [S1]. The dispatcher\u2019s role is explicitly to \u201cavoid duplicated effort\u201d in this architecture.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "nm-01", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S13", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S14", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S15", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S16", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 10123, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q04", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "An assistant can recall old notes without a huge context window by using **external memory systems** that retrieve only the relevant parts on demand.\n\n1. **Paged long-term memory (MemGPT)** \u2013 A persistent memory store holds notes from earlier sessions. At inference time, a ranking/retrieval step selects the most relevant notes and pages them into the model\u2019s small context window, so the assistant \u201cremembers\u201d without ever loading the full history [S1].\n\n2. **Fixed-size recurrent memory (State Space Models)** \u2013 Architectures such as state space models maintain a constant-size internal state while scanning a sequence. This gives linear compute cost and strong long-range recall, allowing the model to carry information from far-back tokens without expanding the context window [S6].\n\nBoth approaches avoid the quadratic cost of full attention over a massive context by keeping the active context small and fetching or compressing older information as needed.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5057, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q05", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a lab blog post, a sandbox limits what a program can read or write, and permissions decide which capabilities the runtime may grant; container isolation contains a misbehaving process [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4736, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q06", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Planning breaks a goal into ordered steps before any action begins, which lets a planner revise the plan when a step fails [S1]. The outcome is then checked by a verifier that evaluates whether each step succeeded [S1]; in coding tasks this verification is automated\u2014a test runner scores patches automatically [S5].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 6933, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q07", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Self-correction works when the critic is grounded in a checkable signal [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-04", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dec-01", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4723, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q08", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Based on the corpus, strict spending limits are enforced through **token budgets** that halt spending when a run reaches its cap, and by **cost-measurement tools** that let the agent respond to stay within budget. One system (LedgerGuard) detects overruns after they occur rather than preventing them.\n\n- A token budget \u201cstops spending once a run reaches its cap\u201d [S1] (lab_blog).\n- Tools \u201cmeasure the cost and the agent responds\u201d to avoid overruns [S2] (vetted_preprint).\n- LedgerGuard \u201cflags runs that exceed their budget,\u201d which is a detection mechanism rather than a preventive one [S3] (lab_blog).", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5402, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q09", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Before a dangerous (high-impact) step runs, a **human-in-the-loop review pauses the workflow**; the reviewer sees the proposed action and its evidence, and the workflow resumes only after approval [S8].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4659, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q10", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a peer-reviewed benchmark study, **error accumulation and context limits cause most failures** in long-horizon tasks that require hundreds of sequential steps [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5175, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q11", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Telemetry (observability/tracing) shows where a program gets stuck or loops by recording every model call, tool call, and latency as spans; the resulting traces expose where a run stalled or looped [S10].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-06", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-12", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "search_corpus", "search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 11033, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q12", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a peer-reviewed paper on defending agents against prompt injection in retrieved data, the defense is to **label untrusted content and refuse to follow instructions found inside it** [S1]. The paper explains that prompt injection hides instructions in a web page or document that the model later reads, and this labeling approach mitigates the risk.", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ag-16", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-10", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item"], "tokens": 4879, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q13", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "According to a vetted preprint on deepfake speech detection across unseen speakers, spoofed speech detection must generalize to voices it never trained on, and the paper indicates that front\u2011end features and data augmentation reduce the \u201cspeaker shortcut\u201d that otherwise hurts generalization to unseen speakers [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-15", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "dc-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "dc-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-09", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ml-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "nm-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "search_corpus", "search_corpus"], "tokens": 10051, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q14", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Sparse attention** reduces the quadratic cost of full attention by attending only to a subset of positions; routing mechanisms select the keys that matter for each query [S2].\n\n**State space models (SSMs)** replace attention with a recurrent scan that maintains a fixed-size memory (state), yielding linear cost in sequence length while preserving long-range recall [S1].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ag-07", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-17", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ag-08", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "dec-05", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-18", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 5043, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q15", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "**Mixture-of-experts routing** changes the transformer by activating only a subset of feed-forward blocks for each token, rather than all blocks, with a learned router that balances computational load and model quality [S1].\n\n**Rotary positional encodings (RoPE)** change the transformer by injecting position information through rotating query and key vectors, rather than adding positional embeddings, and scaling the rotation enables longer context lengths [S2].", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "ml-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "ml-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "ml-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "ag-05", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}], "tools": ["search_corpus", "get_item", "get_item"], "tokens": 6916, "provider_error": false}
{"question_id": "q16", "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free", "set_version": 1, "answer_text": "Text watermarking and attacking an image watermark are fundamentally different activities\u2014one is a **defensive embedding technique**, the other an **adversarial evasion technique**.\n\n**Text watermarking** (defensive, constructive): During text generation, a secret key biases the model\u2019s token choices so that a statistical signal is embedded in the output. A detector who knows the key can later recover that signal to prove the text was machine-generated [S1].\n\n**Attacking an image watermark** (offensive, adversarial): After a watermarked image has been produced, an attacker perturbs the image (e.g., adds noise, crops, compresses) until the watermark detector fails to detect the embedded signal. Robustness is evaluated against such perturbations [S3].\n\nIn short:\n- **Goal**: embedding provenance vs. removing/evading provenance  \n- **When applied**: at generation time (text) vs. post-generation (image)  \n- **Mechanism**: secret-key token bias vs. image perturbation  \n- **Modality**: discrete token sequences vs. continuous pixel data", "sources": [{"alias": "S1", "external_id": "af-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S2", "external_id": "af-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S3", "external_id": "af-05", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S4", "external_id": "af-01", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S5", "external_id": "af-06", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S6", "external_id": "ag-14", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S7", "external_id": "nm-03", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S8", "external_id": "dec-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S9", "external_id": "af-04", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S10", "external_id": "ml-03", "tier": "peer_reviewed"}, {"alias": "S11", "external_id": "ag-11", "tier": "lab_blog"}, {"alias": "S12", "external_id": "dc-02", "tier": "vetted_preprint"}, {"alias": "S13", "external